            <ArticleTitle>Coronary artery bypass in idiopathic thrombocytopenia without splenectomy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>721-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A patient with coronary artery disease and idiopathic thrombocytopenia purpura underwent coronary artery bypass grafting without splenectomy. Our experience indicates that use of cardiopulmonary bypass in patients with idiopathic thrombocytopenic purpura does not invariably mandate splenectomy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
